Thought-2: Thought-2 (revised): Instead of checking all possible combinations of two additional tiles, prioritize forming a shuntsu by looking for missing tiles in sequences. If no shuntsu can be formed, then consider forming a koutsu by checking for duplicate tiles. This approach ensures that the minimum number of tiles required to complete a mentsu is efficiently determined.
Thought-3: Implement a greedy algorithm to always try to form a shuntsu before considering a koutsu, as shuntsu are generally more flexible.


